Dear Customer,

On <%= @migration_date %>, <%= @display_name %> will transition to a new billing platform for an enhanced billing experience.

What is the new billing platform?

The new billing platform is a suite of new features designed to help you understand and manage your GitHub spend.

Benefits of the new platform include:

- Spend transparency - view usage for organizations, repositories, products, and SKUs by hour, day, month, or year
- Improved control - set budgets to limit spending and configure alerts to stay informed of budget utilization

For more information, refer to "<%= @using_billing_platform_url %>".

What to expect:

You will gain access to the new billing experience on <%= @migration_date %>.

- Once transitioned, a new Billing & Licensing section will appear in your account settings.
- Spending limits will be migrated and recreated as budgets in the new billing experience. For more details about budgets, visit "<%= @billing_platform_budget_url %>"
- Historical usage will not be visible in the new billing experience. You will still be able to see historical usage by generating a usage report.

Important changes:

- Git Large File Storage will transition from prepaid, quota-based data packs to a usage-based metered billing model. Credits will be issued for any unused data packs. For more information, visit "<%= @billing_platform_lfs_url %>"
- Some billing-related APIs will no longer work or will work differently. For more information about API changes, visit "<%= @billing_platform_rest_api_url %>"

You're receiving this email because you're an owner of <%= @display_name %> on GitHub.
